   "evidence": "Strip.lean:121-127 states `(hb : f =O[\ud835\udcdd[>] 0] fun x => x ^ (-b)) (hN : b < N.re) : MellinDisConvergent f N` \u2014 a single implication, with no converse and no definition of the abscissa; `grep -r abscissa code/EpsilonEridani` finds only these docstrings, no declaration.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/Convolution/Strip.lean",
   "fix": "Retitle to something matching the conclusion, e.g. \"**Convergence from the small-`x` bound.**\" and rename the section to \"## Convergence and holomorphy from the small-`x` behaviour\"; reserve \"abscissa\" for a declaration that actually defines `sInf {\u03c3 | MellinDisConvergent f \u03c3}` and computes it.",
   "issue": "`mellinDisConvergent_of_isBigO_rpow` carries the bold title \"**The abscissa of convergence.**\" (and sits under the section header \"## The abscissa of convergence and the small-`x` behaviour\", line 84; cf. the module docstring \"whose abscissa is fixed by the behaviour of `f` as `x \u2192 0`\", line 21). No abscissa is defined anywhere in the PR, and the theorem proves only that `f =O[\ud835\udcdd[>] 0] (\u00b7 ^ (-b))` is sufficient for convergence on `b < Re N` \u2014 it does not identify `b` as the abscissa (e.g. `f = 0` satisfies the hypothesis for every `b` yet converges everywhere). In Mathlib \"abscissa of convergence\" is a defined quantity (`abscissaOfAbsConv`, Mathlib/NumberTheory/LSeries/Convergence.lean), so the title advertises a result that is not proved.",
   "line": "121"
  }
 ],
